.TH CVECTOR_AT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_at \- access an element at a specific index
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

void *cvector_at(cvec v, size_t index);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Gives a pointer to the element at the given index, through which the
caller can read the element or change it in place.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v      Vector to access
index  Zero-based index of the element to access
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the element at the index on success.
NULL when index >= elem_count, and when the vector is empty.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1). The pointer is valid only until the size of the vector changes. The
function asserts when v is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_at (3),
.BR cvector_elem_count (3)
